":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree"],"title":"Sorted sets","anchor":"Sorted-sets","generated":true}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A sorted set kept in a treap: a binary search tree whose vertices also carry random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"priorities, with no vertex of higher priority than its parent (Seidel and Aragon, 1996).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The random priorities make the shape that of a random binary search tree, whatever order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements arrive in, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time. A treap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also splits at an element into the elements below it and the rest, and joins two treaps whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements don’t interleave. The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed by rank like an array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treap[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The priorities come from a random number generator given at creation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The treap draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"priorities as its original.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"text":" links, so the treap holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/Treap/height":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap\/height","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/height","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"height","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"title":"height","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of elements on the longest path from the root down: 0 when empty, 1 for one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element, and O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected. The treap does not record it, so reading it walks every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex. O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/SK":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","title":"Swift.BidirectionalCollection"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/Treap/BidirectionalCollection-Implementations":{"kind":"article","title":"BidirectionalCollection Implementations","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap\/bidirectionalcollection-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/BidirectionalCollection-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup